Repository:
  ~/AthenaFusionx

You are auditing BEFORE making any changes.

DO NOT:
- modify any source files
- create repair scripts
- create backups
- run ./nexus.sh
- run a live mission
- revert anything
- make unrelated cleanup changes

The proposed change is to make package-scoped compiler failure iterative:
keep the failed mutation on disk for up to 3 corrective strategist iterations,
feed the real compiler diagnostic back to the strategist, and revert only
after the retry budget is exhausted.

==================================================
1. CURRENT COMPILER FAILURE PATH
==================================================

Inspect the exact compiler-critic failure branch in:

  crates/runtime_core/src/cortical_loop.rs

Show approximately 100 lines surrounding the package-scoped cargo-check
failure handling.

Determine exactly what currently happens after:

  cargo check --manifest-path ... -p <package>

returns nonzero.

Specifically identify:
- mutation rollback
- local_evidence truncation
- graph updates
- returned CortexState

==================================================
2. STATE LIFETIME
==================================================

Trace:

  compiler failure
      -> CortexState::Strategize
      -> strategist prompt construction
      -> next action
      -> Execute
      -> compiler verification

Inspect every place that modifies:

  session.local_evidence

Determine whether evidence survives a Strategize transition.

Find all:
  truncate(...)
  clear()
  assignment/replacement
  prompt truncation

Do not assume the last 2,500 characters are sufficient.

Report the exact behavior.

==================================================
3. RETRY COUNTER SAFETY
==================================================

Evaluate the proposed mechanism:

  session.local_evidence
      .matches("[COMPILE_FAIL_ITERATION")
      .count()

Determine whether this count is:

A. reliably scoped to the current mutation/node/session
or
B. vulnerable to counting an earlier unrelated compiler failure.

Also determine whether local_evidence can be truncated in a way that resets
the count before the three retries are exhausted.

If unsafe, recommend the smallest state-local alternative.

==================================================
4. FAILED SOURCE RETENTION
==================================================

Trace every possible rollback path after compiler failure.

Determine whether returning:

  CortexState::Strategize

while leaving the failed mutation on disk actually preserves that source
until the next PatchFunction.

Check:

- compiler critic
- CortexState transitions
- executor
- DAG/node handling
- any automatic git checkout
- sovereign_core compiler gates
- other rollback helpers

Report every path that could restore the file.

==================================================
5. ANTI-LOOP INTERACTION
==================================================

Inspect:

  CorticalLoop::action_key

and the live anti-loop logic.

Confirm:

same path + function + same new_body
    => same key

same path + function + different new_body
    => different key

different reasoning + same new_body
    => same key

Then determine whether a corrective PatchFunction after a compile failure
can actually execute when it supplies a different body.

This is a REQUIRED safety check.

==================================================
6. COMPILER ERROR DELIVERY
==================================================

Inspect strategist prompt construction.

Determine whether:

  [COMPILE_FAIL_ITERATION N]
  [COMPILE_FAIL_ACTION]
  [COMPILE_FAIL_DETAIL]

plus the actual rustc diagnostic will reliably reach the next strategist
turn.

Pay particular attention to:
- prompt truncation
- evidence ordering
- newest-vs-oldest evidence
- maximum prompt size

Do not merely state that it "should" survive.

==================================================
7. BELIEF GRAPH EFFECT
==================================================

Inspect the proposed:

  EdgeRelation::Contradicts
  confidence 0.30

retry behavior.

Determine whether repeated:

  session.graph.propagate_beliefs()

can effectively kill the current hypothesis before three retries are
available.

Compare this with the existing stronger failure behavior.

Report whether -0.30 is safe, excessive, or insufficient.

==================================================
8. BUDGET SEMANTICS
==================================================

The intended contract is:

iteration 1:
  keep mutation
  expose compiler error
  Strategize

iteration 2:
  keep mutation
  expose compiler error
  Strategize

iteration 3:
  keep mutation
  expose compiler error
  Strategize

next failure after budget:
  revert mutation
  return Strategize

Verify whether the proposed:

  prior_iterations >= COMPILE_RETRY_BUDGET

actually implements that exact contract.

Identify any off-by-one issue.

==================================================
9. SUCCESS PATH
==================================================

Confirm that a successful corrective compile still follows the existing
success contract:

  [COMPILE_OK]

and that no retry-specific marker interferes with:
- PatchMarkerAcquired
- DAG completion
- node verification
- Cortex terminal state

==================================================
10. EXISTING TEST COVERAGE
==================================================

Find existing compiler-critic and cortical-loop tests.

Determine whether there is currently a test capable of proving:

1. failed compile does NOT immediately revert
2. compiler diagnostic is retained
3. retry counter increments
4. different PatchFunction body can execute
5. success after retry completes normally
6. fourth failure reverts

Do not add tests yet.

==================================================
11. ARBITER SECURITY
==================================================

Do not modify arbiter_agent.rs.

Simply confirm that the separate compound-command security repair is
independent of this compiler-retry change.

==================================================
12. FINAL VERDICT
==================================================

Return exactly one:

  SAFE TO INSTALL AS WRITTEN

  SAFE TO INSTALL WITH SURGICAL CHANGES

  DO NOT INSTALL

If surgical changes are required, provide:
- exact issue
- why it matters
- smallest fix
- exact location
- required regression test

Do not write a repair script yet.

Do not modify the repository.

Do not run a live mission.

